1
00:00:06,677 --> 00:00:11,546
<font color="#4096d1"> -==www.RagBear.com==- 是, 首相  第2季第3集

2
00:00:13,803 --> 00:00:18,747
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:24,879 --> 00:00:31,970
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译&校对&时间轴: Tpring

4
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:38,929
外交事件

5
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:44,271
汉弗莱 我们得谈谈海峡隧道
Humphrey, we've got to discuss this ceremony for

6
00:00:44,271 --> 00:00:46,809
奠基典礼宣传的事      好的
the start of work on the Channel Tunnel.

7
00:00:46,809 --> 00:00:49,169
外交部又在拖延了
The Foreign Office is stalling.

8
00:00:49,169 --> 00:00:51,896
他们说协议条文还没敲定呢
They say things still haven't been finalised.

9
00:00:51,896 --> 00:00:54,724
也该完了 头等大事啊
About time they were. Big occasion.

10
00:00:54,890 --> 00:01:01,489
大门揭幕 尊敬的首相吉姆哈克亲手奠基
the laying of the foundation stone by the PM, James Hacker.

11
00:01:01,650 --> 00:01:06,644
"我们两大民主国家世代相连"(丘吉尔)
This historic link between our two great sovereign democracies.

12
00:01:06,810 --> 00:01:09,011
重大新闻      可外交部
Great coverage. F.O.

13
00:01:09,011 --> 00:01:10,868
还没和法国谈妥呢
Haven't agreed everything with the French.

14
00:01:10,868 --> 00:01:12,564
对 我看唯一办法
The only solution is for me to

15
00:01:12,564 --> 00:01:14,908
只有找法国总统作高峰会谈
have a meeting with the French president

16
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:16,876
由我亲自商定了
and sort it out myself.

17
00:01:19,770 --> 00:01:24,480
我真没想到 您在考虑如此激进的手段
I didn't know you were considering such a stimulating approach.

18
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:25,362
我想好了
Well, I am.

19
00:01:25,362 --> 00:01:30,218
首相 您觉得您个人有能力与法国谈判吗?
Are you capable of concluding this negotiation?

20
00:01:30,218 --> 00:01:32,885
有什么难的 关键分歧在哪?
What are the outstanding points?

21
00:01:32,885 --> 00:01:34,791
他们主要担心主权问题
Mainly they're concerned with sovereignty.

22
00:01:34,791 --> 00:01:37,028
您认为边界应该在哪?
Where do you believe the frontier should be?

23
00:01:37,028 --> 00:01:39,191
边界?      英国和法国的边界
The frontier between Britain and France.

24
00:01:39,690 --> 00:01:42,488
现在的位置有什么不好?
What's wrong with wherever it is now?

25
00:01:42,650 --> 00:01:46,484
领海界限各三海里 隧道中央归谁?
The three-mile limit. Who would own the middle of the tunnel?

26
00:01:47,570 --> 00:01:51,529
您看 英国的立场是一边一半
The British position is that we should own half each.

27
00:01:51,690 --> 00:01:55,285
挺公平啊      对 可法国人不觉得公平
That seems fair. The French don't think it's fair.

28
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,804
他们希望边界设在多佛港(英国)
They want the frontier to be at Dover.

29
00:01:57,804 --> 00:01:59,192
岂有此理
Ridiculous.

30
00:01:59,192 --> 00:02:02,685
列车的主权又归谁?
Who would have sovereignty over the trains?

31
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:05,522
如果法国列车上发生罪案
If a crime was committed on a French train

32
00:02:05,522 --> 00:02:08,083
在英国地段 司法权归英国还是法国?
in the British sector, who'd have jurisdiction?

33
00:02:08,083 --> 00:02:11,924
英国...不 法国...不 英国
The British. Well... No, the French. No, the British.

34
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:14,995
如果一具尸体从法国地段的
And if a body was pushed out of

35
00:02:14,995 --> 00:02:17,030
英国列车里抛出呢?
a British train in the French sector?

36
00:02:17,030 --> 00:02:20,529
法国吧 不 英国 嗯...
Well, the French. Um... no, the British. Um...

37
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:22,470
如果一台英国卡车装上
If a British lorry was loaded onto

38
00:02:22,470 --> 00:02:25,349
英国地段的法国列车 归谁管呢?
a French train in the British sector?

39
00:02:25,349 --> 00:02:29,006
英国卡车 归英国...或者法国
A British lorry, the British... or the French.

40
00:02:30,570 --> 00:02:33,352
能不能把刑事司法权分成两支
Could jurisdiction be divided into two legs?

41
00:02:33,352 --> 00:02:34,449
内外各一支?
Home and away?

42
00:02:36,026 --> 00:02:37,536
对 谢谢 伯纳
Yes, thank you, Bernard.

43
00:02:37,536 --> 00:02:41,701
隧道中央要立界碑吗?
Should we have a frontier post in the middle of the tunnel?

44
00:02:41,701 --> 00:02:44,170
要啊 呃 不要      立在半道上?
Well, yeah. Er, no. Halfway across?

45
00:02:45,210 --> 00:02:47,551
海关和移民检查
Should we have customs and immigration clearance

46
00:02:47,551 --> 00:02:50,266
设在这边还是那边 还是两边都要?
at one end or the other or both ends?

47
00:02:50,970 --> 00:02:55,009
恕我直言 汉弗莱 这都是律师的事
With respect, these are points for the lawyers to discuss.

48
00:02:55,170 --> 00:02:59,527
正是 首相 可我好像听说您要亲自解决
Precisely, but I thought you wanted to handle it yourself.

49
00:02:59,690 --> 00:03:04,081
当然 我没打算讨论国际法的细枝末节
I don't want to discuss points of abstruse international law.

50
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:06,180
我是想敲定政治问题
I want to get the political points settled.

51
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,744
原来主权不是政治问题啊
So sovereignty's not political?

52
00:03:08,744 --> 00:03:11,244
真有意思
How interesting.

53
00:03:11,410 --> 00:03:15,767
还有路标 法国希望法语在前 英语在后
The French want the signs to be in French first and English second.

54
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:18,808
那可不行      那您就开不成庆典了
No! Then you can't have your ceremony.

55
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:23,361
不如法国那边法语在前 英国英语在前?
Well, French first at the French end?

56
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:26,602
列车上呢?      得了 汉弗莱 这重要吗?
What about on the trains? Oh, does it matter?

57
00:03:26,770 --> 00:03:29,264
法国人觉得重要 菜单呢 法语还是英语?
And the menus? French or English?

58
00:03:29,264 --> 00:03:31,693
不能半途上换一套吗?
Couldn't they be changed halfway?

59
00:03:31,693 --> 00:03:34,244
不行 法国人最顽固不化
No. The French are adamant.

60
00:03:34,410 --> 00:03:37,377
所以英法两国协和式飞机
That is why the British and French Concorde are

61
00:03:37,377 --> 00:03:39,755
都写成法语 末尾有个E
spelt the French way with an E.

62
00:03:39,755 --> 00:03:43,165
我们就没压倒过法国吗?      也有几次
Don't we ever get our way with the French? Sometimes.

63
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:47,528
最近一次是几时?      滑铁卢战役 1815年
When was the last time? Battle of Waterloo, 1815.

64
00:03:47,690 --> 00:03:51,842
当然 法国人可能还会提到劫车问题      劫车?
The French may raise the question of hijacking. Hijacking?

65
00:03:52,010 --> 00:03:54,987
要是恐怖分子劫持列车
What if terrorists hijacked the train and

66
00:03:54,987 --> 00:03:56,530
威胁要炸掉隧道 怎么办?
threatened to blow up the tunnel?

67
00:03:56,530 --> 00:04:00,245
这个让给法国管吧 让他们头疼好了
Give the French jurisdiction over the lot, then it's their problem.

68
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:03,392
您看 首相 要是您主持谈判
If you'd handled the negotiations,

69
00:04:03,392 --> 00:04:06,080
您会把什么都让给法国的
you'd have just handed everything over to the French.

70
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:11,398
不过我以为 法国会耍些下流花招
I personally believe the French will come up with a

71
00:04:11,398 --> 00:04:12,939
来占取主动
totally underhand ploy to gain the advantage.

72
00:04:12,939 --> 00:04:15,523
不过您当然早算到了 首相
But no doubt you've anticipated that.

73
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:19,842
仔细想想 谈判也没必要由我亲自主持吧
I don't think it's necessary for me to conduct these negotiations.

74
00:04:20,010 --> 00:04:24,720
如果非要丧权辱国 交给外交大臣好了
If humiliating concessions have to be made, let the FS make them.

75
00:04:24,890 --> 00:04:28,087
真英明 首相      来杯雪利酒吧 伯纳
Very wise. Let's have a glass of sherry, Bernard.

76
00:04:28,250 --> 00:04:32,448
首相 能谈谈您前任回忆录的问题了吗?
May we discuss the vexed question of your predecessor's memoirs?

77
00:04:32,610 --> 00:04:34,999
老天 又怎么啦?      貌似最末一章
What now? The final chapter

78
00:04:35,170 --> 00:04:38,958
写的是他的辞职和您继任的经过
concerns his resignation and your accession to the premiership.

79
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:41,567
因此他想查阅某些政府文件
He wants access to certain papers.

80
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,481
不能封杀这本胡忆录吗?
Can't we stop these bloody memoirs?

81
00:04:43,481 --> 00:04:47,100
唉 回忆录是种职业病
Memoirs, alas, are an occupational hazard.

82
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,820
最可恨的是他的背叛
It's the betrayal that upsets me.

83
00:04:48,820 --> 00:04:52,239
读到头7章之前 我还当他是朋友呢
Until I'd read the first seven chapters, I thought he was a friend.

84
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:55,208
他怎么能那样说我      哪样?
He says some shocking things. Such as?

85
00:04:55,370 --> 00:04:59,158
他管我叫两面派      太不合适了
He calls me two-faced. That was very wrong.

86
00:05:00,570 --> 00:05:03,562
你承认这不合适?      当然了 干杯
You admit he was wrong? Yes, indeed. Cheers.

87
00:05:03,730 --> 00:05:06,847
毫无保密意识      保密意识?
Unforgivably indiscreet. indiscreet?

88
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:11,279
哦 也不合适      他怎能这样诽谤我?
Oh, and wrong. How can he tell such lies about me?

89
00:05:11,450 --> 00:05:13,459
什么诽谤? 哦 明白了
What lies? Oh, yes, I see.

90
00:05:14,524 --> 00:05:15,888
他能落什么好?
What's in it for him?

91
00:05:15,888 --> 00:05:17,930
打开销路?      不是这个问题
Bestseller? No, it's not that.

92
00:05:18,090 --> 00:05:21,560
他撒谎不是为利益 是天性使然
He lies because it's in his nature.

93
00:05:21,730 --> 00:05:25,723
他阴险 恶毒 卑鄙无耻
He's treacherous, malevolent... and vile.

94
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:27,530
要是他还想要什么爵位
If he thinks he'll get any more honours or

95
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:31,206
公营机构或者王室职位 做梦去吧
quango, he's got another thing coming.

96
00:05:31,206 --> 00:05:33,967
有我在 他休想再沽名钓誉
He's not getting one ounce more recognition!

97
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:37,524
对 这事重要吗? 因为...
Yes. Look, is this important? Because...

98
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:42,369
不会吧 哦
No? Oh.

99
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:47,280
途中去世的? 知道了 谢谢
He was dead on arrival? I see. Thanks.

100
00:05:49,130 --> 00:05:52,679
坏消息 伯纳?      是也不是
Bad news, Bernard? Yes... and no.

101
00:05:52,850 --> 00:05:56,559
您的前任 大不列颠帝国前首相
Your predecessor, the previous Prime Minster of Great Britain,

102
00:05:56,730 --> 00:05:59,119
刚才突发心脏病去世了
has just died of a heart attack.

103
00:06:09,130 --> 00:06:11,485
悲剧啊      悲剧悲剧
Tragic. Tragic.

104
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:14,405
他是位伟人      伟人伟人
He was a great man. Great man.

105
00:06:14,570 --> 00:06:17,084
他会永垂不朽的      永垂不朽
He'll be sorely missed. Sorely missed.

106
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:20,401
他的回忆录也是      永远完不成了
So will his memoirs. Which will never be finished.

107
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:22,959
唉      唉
Alas. Alas.

108
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:30,164
似乎在临终前 他说希望以国礼下葬
he expressed a hope that he might have a state funeral.

109
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:32,994
不过既然您不想让他沽名钓誉...
But in view of your wish to pay him no...

110
00:06:32,994 --> 00:06:35,606
不 伯纳 不 你误会我了
No, you must have misunderstood me.

111
00:06:35,606 --> 00:06:39,020
我相信会有很多人想给他送葬的
Many people will want to attend his funeral.

112
00:06:39,020 --> 00:06:40,933
来向一位伟大首相致敬
To pay tribute to a great Prime Minister?

113
00:06:40,933 --> 00:06:42,848
对...
Yeah...

114
00:06:43,010 --> 00:06:45,399
顺便确认他真的死了
...and to make sure he's dead.

115
00:06:47,610 --> 00:06:52,206
7名英联邦首相 美国副总统
Seven Commonwealth Prime Ministers, the American Vice President,

116
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:54,565
俄国外交部长 6名欧洲各国首相
six European Prime Ministers.

117
00:06:54,730 --> 00:06:57,290
真不错      非常不错 首相
Pretty good. Very good, Prime Minister.

118
00:06:57,450 --> 00:07:00,647
我是东道主      正是这样
I am the host. Yes, indeed.

119
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:04,439
各国领袖簇拥 世界舞台中央
Amongst all the world's leaders, centre of the world stage.

120
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:08,762
庄重又不失尊严 强忍悲痛      可不是
Bearing your grief with dignity and fortitude. Quite.

121
00:07:10,090 --> 00:07:13,400
庄重的悲痛很能刺激支持率
Dignified grief goes down very well with the voters,

122
00:07:13,570 --> 00:07:16,562
尤其在全世界政治家烘托之下
especially when it's shared by world statesmen.

123
00:07:16,730 --> 00:07:19,119
死亡真是一件盛事
It's a wonderful thing, death.

124
00:07:20,370 --> 00:07:24,966
让大家同心同德 法国总理又有什么事?
What's this query against the French Prime Minister?

125
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:27,883
我想法国大使马上会来跟您谈
The French ambassador's coming to see you.

126
00:07:28,050 --> 00:07:30,518
会全方位多角度拍摄吧?      是啊
Plenty of room for TV cameras.

127
00:07:30,690 --> 00:07:34,365
10号门口 沿途夹道 修道院里里外外
Outside No.10, outside the abbey, inside the abbey.

128
00:07:34,530 --> 00:07:36,885
安排一台正对着我的座位
One pointing directly at my pew.

129
00:07:37,050 --> 00:07:41,840
那摄影师不就得站在布道坛里吗?
Um... wouldn't that mean putting the cameraman in the pulpit?

130
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:46,120
没问题的吧?
Will that be all right?

131
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:51,719
那大主教就有点站不开了
It won't leave a lot of room for the Archbishop.

132
00:07:52,810 --> 00:07:55,722
他要从哪里布道?
Well... So where will he preach from?

133
00:07:59,330 --> 00:08:02,925
貌似他得站在布道坛里      那我的摄影机摆哪里?
He'll need to be in the pulpit. Where will my camera be?

134
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:05,724
倒还有个主祭台
There's always the high altar,

135
00:08:05,724 --> 00:08:09,075
不过估计大主教也要用的
but I think the Archbishop may need that as well.

136
00:08:09,330 --> 00:08:11,560
他以为他是谁啊?
Who does he think he is?

137
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:14,885
他大概以为这是宗教仪式
He thinks it's a religious ceremony.

138
00:08:14,885 --> 00:08:17,037
没人告诉他这是政党聚会
Nobody's told him it's a party political.

139
00:08:18,050 --> 00:08:20,466
伯纳 法国大使来了吧?
The French ambassador here, is he?

140
00:08:20,466 --> 00:08:22,587
他马上到 可我能先说句话吗?
Yes, but could I have a word first?

141
00:08:22,587 --> 00:08:25,407
法国首相不来了 换法国总统来
The French PM isn't coming. The President's coming instead.

142
00:08:25,570 --> 00:08:28,329
总统? 太棒了      不 首相 糟糕透了
President? Marvellous! No, it's terrible!

143
00:08:28,329 --> 00:08:31,660
怎么?      女王3年前访法时
When the Queen visited France,

144
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:33,433
送过总统一条拉布拉多狗
she presented him with a Labrador puppy.

145
00:08:33,433 --> 00:08:36,282
现在它生小狗了 他要回赠一条      不
Now he's bringing her one of its puppies. No!

146
00:08:36,450 --> 00:08:38,566
恐怕是真的      我说吧
Afraid so. I knew it!

147
00:08:38,730 --> 00:08:41,298
怎么了 这不是向我们示好吗?
It seems to be rather a nice gesture.

148
00:08:41,298 --> 00:08:43,707
是示意 不过不是示好
It's a gesture, but hardly a nice one.

149
00:08:43,707 --> 00:08:45,485
怎么讲?      女王必须拒绝
Why not? She'll have to refuse it.

150
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,845
为什么?      隔离检疫啊 首相
Why? Quarantine!

151
00:08:48,010 --> 00:08:49,988
狗不能随便进口
You can't import dogs!

152
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:52,864
必须在机场隔离检疫6个月
It'll have to spend six months in quarantine.

153
00:08:52,864 --> 00:08:55,248
老天 法国人会理解的 对吧?
The French will understand, won't they?

154
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:58,509
他们私下里理解 所以才耍这花招
They'll understand it privately,

155
00:08:58,509 --> 00:09:00,491
可他们官方拒绝理解
but they'll refuse to understand it officially.

156
00:09:00,491 --> 00:09:02,928
外交部得想想办法 去找彼得      是
The Foreign Office must sort it out. Get Peter.

157
00:09:03,090 --> 00:09:07,214
汉弗莱 他们想引发外交事件
Humphrey, they're creating a diplomatic incident

158
00:09:07,214 --> 00:09:09,971
好夺取海峡隧道的主动权
so they can get their own way over the tunnel.

159
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:13,202
原来如此 首相
Of course, Prime Minister!

160
00:09:14,370 --> 00:09:16,565
彼得 你听说了吧?      对 首相
Peter, you've heard the news? Yes.

161
00:09:16,730 --> 00:09:18,960
我们怎么办?      我不知道
What are we going to do? I don't know.

162
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:21,360
你是我的外交部长啊
You're my Foreign Affairs Secretary.

163
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:24,886
对 我们在想办法变通 可检疫归内政部管
Yes, but the Home Office is responsible for quarantine.

164
00:09:25,050 --> 00:09:28,281
去找格拉汉 不能让他们收回礼物吗?
Get Graham. Can't you get them to withdraw this gift?

165
00:09:28,450 --> 00:09:31,394
我们都试过了 提议改成狗的画像
We've suggested a painting of the puppy,

166
00:09:31,394 --> 00:09:34,358
铜像 瓷像 全都碰了壁
a bronze, a porcelain model. Not a hope.

167
00:09:34,358 --> 00:09:36,922
不能让他们填起来吗?      什么...
Couldn't you get them to stuff it? Well...

168
00:09:37,090 --> 00:09:39,558
哦 做成标本 不行 没戏
Oh, taxidermy. No, no chance.

169
00:09:39,730 --> 00:09:42,194
格拉汉 内政部得想办法
Tell the Home Office they

170
00:09:42,194 --> 00:09:44,185
绕过检疫规章
must find a way round quarantine regulations.

171
00:09:44,185 --> 00:09:47,002
恐怕办不到 首相      为什么?
Out of the question. What do you mean?

172
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:49,922
首先这条规章我们对一切国民
We enforce them vigorously with all British citizens

173
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:52,936
和世界各国都不通融
and foreign nationals.

174
00:09:52,936 --> 00:09:55,725
再说检疫法是女王亲笔签署的
Also the Quarantine Act is signed by the Queen.

175
00:09:55,890 --> 00:09:59,599
她不能专对自己法外开恩啊 办不到
She can't be the only one to break her own laws.

176
00:10:00,570 --> 00:10:04,688
法国大使来了 首相      要他先等一会
The French ambassador's here. Ask him to wait for a moment.

177
00:10:04,850 --> 00:10:07,616
回外交部去 叫他们和内政部商量
Get back to the Foreign Office.

178
00:10:07,616 --> 00:10:09,519
必须想办法变通
Say we've got to find a way round this.

179
00:10:09,519 --> 00:10:12,716
你们都跟伯纳保持联络 伯纳 你联络皇宫
Keep in touch with Bernard.

180
00:10:12,716 --> 00:10:16,050
汉弗莱 你找法务部 统筹协调 好吗?
Bernard, liaise with the palace. Humphrey, coordinate it all.

181
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:18,429
我会在内阁办公室设个通讯室
I'll set up an operations room.

182
00:10:18,429 --> 00:10:19,657
我们还得做什么?
Anything else we ought to do?

183
00:10:19,657 --> 00:10:21,449
我想您该见法国大使了 首相
I think you should see the ambassador now.

184
00:10:21,449 --> 00:10:22,942
好 叫他进来
OK, wheel him in.

185
00:10:22,942 --> 00:10:25,099
不许走 汉弗莱 留下给我打气
Don't you go, Humphrey!

186
00:10:25,099 --> 00:10:26,753
要我准备文件吗?
Do I need any papers?

187
00:10:26,753 --> 00:10:28,640
不用 准备海绵绷带就好
No, just a sponge and a towel.

188
00:10:29,410 --> 00:10:33,119
法国大使阁下到      大使阁下
His Excellency, the French ambassador. Excellency.

189
00:10:33,290 --> 00:10:36,403
首相 多谢您拨冗与我会晤
You're most kind to give me your time.

190
00:10:36,403 --> 00:10:38,079
(法语)万分荣幸
Enchant?

191
00:10:39,370 --> 00:10:43,079
听说您急着要敲定海峡隧道协议?
You're anxious to finalise the agreement for the tunnel?

192
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:45,810
可不是 老实说...
Very much so. In fact...

193
00:10:45,970 --> 00:10:49,679
也不算急 当然如果...      当然
There's no real hurry. It would be nice if... Quite.

194
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:53,638
我国政府认为 如果我们借这次葬礼...
My government feels that if we took advantage of the funeral...

195
00:10:53,810 --> 00:10:58,520
我个人谨表哀悼 悲剧啊      悲剧悲剧
My condolences, by the way. A tragic loss. Oh, tragic, tragic.

196
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:01,671
如果我们借这次葬礼
If we took advantage of the funeral

197
00:11:01,671 --> 00:11:03,964
让您和我国总统面谈...
for you and our President to speak...

198
00:11:03,964 --> 00:11:07,400
对 当然 不过还有好多
Of course, I will be host to a

199
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,853
重要人物出席 我不太好安排
large number of distinguished people. It may not be easy.

200
00:11:10,853 --> 00:11:12,643
您不想和我们总统谈话?
You do not wish to speak to our President?

201
00:11:12,810 --> 00:11:17,645
不不不 当然...想也不想
Oh, yes, yes, yes, of course. Well, yes... and no.

202
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:20,529
谈话当然可以 不过谈判...
Speak, yes, of course, but negotiate...

203
00:11:20,690 --> 00:11:23,948
您不觉得这种友邻之争
Don't you think these quarrels between friends

204
00:11:23,948 --> 00:11:27,797
最好由当面对话解决吗?
are best resolved by just talking together?

205
00:11:27,797 --> 00:11:29,730
友邻之间 没错
Between friends, yes.

206
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:31,963
不然总统可要伤心了
Otherwise the President may be hurt.

207
00:11:31,963 --> 00:11:34,963
个人倒没什么 可他是代表全法国受辱
Not personally, but as a snub to France.

208
00:11:34,963 --> 00:11:37,085
不不 绝无此意 我们是世交好友
No intention. Great friends.

209
00:11:37,250 --> 00:11:42,278
太好了 第二个问题是访问期间使团的安全
The second point is the security of our embassy during the visit.

210
00:11:42,450 --> 00:11:44,680
对 警察厅长说都安排妥了
Yes, everything's in hand.

211
00:11:44,850 --> 00:11:49,446
我国政府要求批准法国警方随团护卫
requests that the French police be permitted to guard

212
00:11:49,610 --> 00:11:52,016
法国警方? 怎么可能
French police? No, that's not possible.

213
00:11:52,016 --> 00:11:54,190
也不一定不可能吧
It is surely not impossible?

214
00:11:54,190 --> 00:11:55,911
你们不信任英国警方吗?
Don't you trust the British police?

215
00:11:55,911 --> 00:11:58,358
我国政府对英国警方不做评价
We make no comment on the British police.

216
00:11:58,970 --> 00:12:03,839
但我们总统更希望让法国警方来管
But our President want the French police were in charge.

217
00:12:04,010 --> 00:12:07,045
您看 阁下 问题是
The problem, Excellency, is that

218
00:12:07,045 --> 00:12:09,971
届时会有一百多个使团来到伦敦
there are well over a hundred embassies in London.

219
00:12:09,971 --> 00:12:12,573
大家当然都想用自己的警察
No doubt they'd all want their own police.

220
00:12:12,573 --> 00:12:14,878
大多数警察会带机关枪
Most of them would carry machine guns.

221
00:12:14,878 --> 00:12:17,880
女皇政府并不完全相信...
Her Majesty's government is not... totally convinced

222
00:12:18,050 --> 00:12:21,042
这会让伦敦更加安全
that that would make London a safer place.

223
00:12:21,850 --> 00:12:24,887
那我国政府要大失所望了
My government will be most disappointed.

224
00:12:25,890 --> 00:12:28,688
好在我还有件愉快的事
But now I can turn to a happy matter.

225
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:34,720
我国总统会带来一件小礼物 赠给女皇陛下
Our President will be bringing a little present to Her Majesty.

226
00:12:34,890 --> 00:12:38,290
真周到      一条小狗
How charming. A little puppy.

227
00:12:39,249 --> 00:12:40,952
她名叫"小砂锅"
Her name is Cocotte.

228
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:43,007
"小砂锅"
Cocotte.

229
00:12:44,250 --> 00:12:46,851
生它的那条拉布拉多犬正是
She comes from the litter of the same Labrador that

230
00:12:46,851 --> 00:12:50,366
女王上次访法时
Her Majesty presented to the President

231
00:12:50,366 --> 00:12:53,139
慷慨赠给总统的
on her last state visit to France.

232
00:12:54,530 --> 00:12:57,567
可以通报他赠送仪式的安排吗?
Let him know the arrangements for the presentation.

233
00:12:57,730 --> 00:13:00,026
当然 你们太周到了
Oh, delightful thought.

234
00:13:00,026 --> 00:13:03,859
可惜赠送仪式6个月内不能举行
The presentation won't be possible for another six months.

235
00:13:03,859 --> 00:13:06,128
我国检疫法的规定      岂有此理
Our quarantine laws. Absurd.

236
00:13:06,290 --> 00:13:09,352
贵国女王来访时带了条狗
Your Queen gave her dog during her visit.

237
00:13:09,352 --> 00:13:11,711
为什么我国总统就不行?
Why can our President not do the same?

238
00:13:11,711 --> 00:13:14,025
对 承蒙好意 我们其实非常...
Delightful thought, nothing we'd rather...

239
00:13:14,025 --> 00:13:15,225
不过国有国法
but the law is the law.

240
00:13:15,225 --> 00:13:20,802
法律当然是防范带病动物的吧?      对...
Surely it exists to exclude infected animals? Er... yes.

241
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:25,964
您是暗示法国总统会向英国女王赠送
Do you suggest the President of France would present

242
00:13:26,130 --> 00:13:28,325
一条病狗?
with a diseased puppy?

243
00:13:29,330 --> 00:13:31,924
不不不...      那就这么定了
No, no, no... Then it is settled.

244
00:13:32,090 --> 00:13:34,687
不 不能定 恐怕您必须
No, it is not. Suggest to your

245
00:13:34,687 --> 00:13:36,625
建议总统换别的礼物
President that he brings a different gift.

246
00:13:36,625 --> 00:13:40,046
办不到 要说总统本人 还有希望
Out of the question. Were it the President alone, perhaps.

247
00:13:40,210 --> 00:13:45,068
但总统夫人 我国第一夫人决意要送
The President's wife, our first lady, has set her heart on it.

248
00:13:45,068 --> 00:13:46,452
她已经认准了
She is determined.

249
00:13:46,452 --> 00:13:49,007
我们会尽力而为 不过恐怕无能为力
We'll make every effort, but it may not be possible.

250
00:13:49,170 --> 00:13:53,960
首相 我国政府将感到莫名惊诧和严重受辱
I cannot tell you the gravity my government would feel

251
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:57,252
如果女王陛下居然拒收她本人
if Her Majesty were to refuse a gift in exchange

252
00:13:57,252 --> 00:14:00,145
赠给总统礼物的回礼
for the one our President accepted from her.

253
00:14:00,145 --> 00:14:03,419
恐怕这不仅会被看作有辱国体
I fear it would be interpreted as both a national

254
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:07,241
更会冒犯总统个人及其夫人
and a personal affront to the President and his wife.

255
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:13,443
阁下 您得劝总统别带那条母狗来
you must ask the President not to bring that bitch with him.

256
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:18,408
不不 那条小狗
No, no, the puppy.

257
00:14:18,570 --> 00:14:20,561
我是说小狗
I meant the puppy.

258
00:14:23,290 --> 00:14:25,281
还得单独安排夫人们的行程
We have to lay on visits for the wives.

259
00:14:25,450 --> 00:14:28,647
外交部喜欢这样 好把她们全撇开
The Foreign Office like it. Keeps them out of the way.

260
00:14:28,810 --> 00:14:31,802
干吗不让她们陪同丈夫?      丈夫忙着呢
Why can't they be with their husbands? They're busy.

261
00:14:31,970 --> 00:14:35,440
只是葬礼上罢了      安妮 他们不是来送葬的
Only at the funeral. They're not coming for the funeral.

262
00:14:35,610 --> 00:14:39,762
是来谈政务的 这是一次工作葬礼
They're coming here for the politics. This is a working funeral.

263
00:14:39,930 --> 00:14:44,879
上回挪威的国葬 法国 德国和我都忙着
At that funeral in Norway, the French, Germans and I,

264
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:48,201
谈进出口配额问题 连教堂都忘去了
talking about quotas, we forgot to go to the cathedral.

265
00:14:48,370 --> 00:14:49,665
他们发现了吗?
Did they notice?

266
00:14:50,647 --> 00:14:52,759
能没发现嘛 我们都迟到了
They noticed, all right. We got there late.

267
00:14:52,930 --> 00:14:56,923
保安背了黑锅 如今什么都能怪保安人员
Blamed security. You can blame security for anything nowadays.

268
00:14:57,090 --> 00:14:59,611
那这次葬礼可以算首脑峰会了?
So this funeral will be a sort of summit.

269
00:14:59,611 --> 00:15:02,488
对 这是天赐良机
Yes. It's a heaven-sent opportunity.

270
00:15:02,488 --> 00:15:04,768
字面上的      对
Literally. Yes.

271
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:08,240
比峰会还好 没有既定目标
Better than a summit because there are no expectations.

272
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:10,686
没人指望领导人从葬礼上搞到
People don't expect leaders to come back with

273
00:15:10,686 --> 00:15:13,560
禁止核试验或者生产限额协定
test-ban agreements or quota reductions,

274
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:16,767
于是我们就能谈些有意义的东西了
so we can have some meaningful discussions.

275
00:15:16,930 --> 00:15:19,704
峰会只算是公关大会
A summit is just a public-relations circus.

276
00:15:19,704 --> 00:15:23,070
就没人是来向老朋友致敬的吗?
Isn't anyone coming to pay tribute to a friend?

277
00:15:23,070 --> 00:15:25,864
朋友? 要是只请他的朋友
A friend? If only his friends came to the abbey,

278
00:15:25,864 --> 00:15:27,609
连小礼拜堂都填不满
we wouldn't even fill the vestry.

279
00:15:29,090 --> 00:15:32,073
他这一死为世界做的贡献
He's done much more for the world by dying

280
00:15:32,073 --> 00:15:33,806
比他活着一辈子都大
than he ever did in the whole of his life.

281
00:15:34,050 --> 00:15:36,041
你敲定仪式细节了吗?
Have you agreed the service?

282
00:15:36,210 --> 00:15:38,405
对 一直奏乐      这倒不错
Yeah, lots of music. That's nice.

283
00:15:38,570 --> 00:15:42,961
嗯 有管风琴掩护 就能谈点有用的了
Mm, you can have useful discussions when the organ's playing.

284
00:15:43,130 --> 00:15:46,759
齐声祷告时就不行      布道的时候呢?
Have to shut up for the lesson. What about the sermon?

285
00:15:46,930 --> 00:15:49,683
那是用来倒时差的
That's when you catch up on jet lag.

286
00:15:51,170 --> 00:15:53,889
没错 这葬礼来得正是时候
This funeral's come at the right moment.

287
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:58,362
有一堆事要谈呢 北约 华沙条约 中东问题
We've all sorts to discuss about NATO, the Warsaw Pact

288
00:15:58,530 --> 00:16:00,964
要是这三天解决不完呢?
And what if you don't sort it all out?

289
00:16:01,130 --> 00:16:03,492
那我们只能盼望
We'll just have to hope that before too long

290
00:16:03,492 --> 00:16:05,774
有别的大人物尽快蹬腿了
somebody else important snuffs it.

291
00:16:07,210 --> 00:16:09,201
对 我跟内政部谈过了
I've spoken to the Home Office.

292
00:16:09,370 --> 00:16:14,160
他们说没理由要求国会为该狗专门立法
there's no grounds to pass an act to for this dog

293
00:16:14,330 --> 00:16:16,924
我知道特许授权法什么都能授权
I know an enabling act can enable anything,

294
00:16:17,090 --> 00:16:18,524
不过首相觉得
but the PM feels it

295
00:16:18,524 --> 00:16:20,620
这只能授权他输掉下次大选
would merely enable him to lose the next election.

296
00:16:21,370 --> 00:16:24,702
伯纳 能不能考虑把整个皇宫
Have you thought of turning Buckingham Palace

297
00:16:24,702 --> 00:16:27,168
变成犬只隔离区?      你说真的?
into a quarantine zone for dogs?

298
00:16:27,168 --> 00:16:28,682
只是个想法罢了
Just a thought.

299
00:16:28,682 --> 00:16:30,120
女王的威尔士矮脚狗呢?
What about the corgis?

300
00:16:30,290 --> 00:16:33,636
稍等 格拉汉 联络皇宫
Hang on. Graham, check with the palace

301
00:16:33,636 --> 00:16:37,194
确认女王没有正式得知礼物的事
that Her Majesty's not been told officially

302
00:16:37,194 --> 00:16:39,726
免得拒收和她扯上关系
this gift then she can't be implicated in refusing it.

303
00:16:39,726 --> 00:16:42,329
对 我们需要同声传译
Yes, we will want simultaneous translators.

304
00:16:42,490 --> 00:16:47,484
不 会见英语国家元首时就免了
not when the PM meets the leaders of English nations.

305
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:51,438
对 英语国家可以包括美国
Yes, they can be said to include the US...

306
00:16:52,650 --> 00:16:55,642
以显示我们的慷慨大度 我得挂了
...with a certain generosity of spirit. Got to go.

307
00:16:55,810 --> 00:17:00,201
对 10国元首专机今天抵达 特工处快疯了
Yes, 10 PMs are flying in today. Special Branch are crazy.

308
00:17:00,370 --> 00:17:04,363
皇家海军乐队也是 得演奏所有的国歌
So is the Royal Marines band who play all the national anthems.

309
00:17:04,530 --> 00:17:08,003
知道了 阿根廷不来了 真走运
I see. Argentina's not coming. A bit of luck.

310
00:17:08,003 --> 00:17:09,648
因为马岛事件?
Because of the Falklands?

311
00:17:09,648 --> 00:17:13,203
不 因为他们的国歌有6分钟长
No, because their anthem goes on for about six minutes.

312
00:17:13,370 --> 00:17:16,362
喂 我知道你担心狗的事 我也是
I know you're worried about this dog. So am I.

313
00:17:16,530 --> 00:17:18,819
跟我们驻巴黎大使说说
Talk to our ambassador in Paris.

314
00:17:18,819 --> 00:17:20,960
看他能不能想法灭了它
See if he can think of a way to nobble it.

315
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:24,802
你知道 下点药什么的
You know, slip it something.

316
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:26,694
问问保加利亚人
See if the Bulgarians have

317
00:17:26,694 --> 00:17:28,505
还有没有毒伞尖 (乔治马可夫案 1978)
got any spare umbrella tips.

318
00:17:29,290 --> 00:17:31,697
伯纳 还有个办法
If we made the palace an extension

319
00:17:31,697 --> 00:17:35,915
把皇宫并入法国大使馆 狗就不算入境了
of the French embassy, the dog would be on foreign territory.

320
00:17:35,915 --> 00:17:38,882
彼得 首相正拼命争取海峡隧道的主权
The PM is fighting for the sovereignty of the tunnel.

321
00:17:39,050 --> 00:17:42,087
把皇宫都让出去他会怎么想?
How would he feel about palace sovereignty?

322
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:44,947
你觉得皇室会怎么想? 喂
How do you think the sovereign would feel?

323
00:17:44,947 --> 00:17:48,262
不 礼堂里不能按字母顺序排位
No, we can't have alphabetical seating in the abbey.

324
00:17:48,262 --> 00:17:51,167
不然伊拉克会挨着伊朗坐
You'd have Iraq and Iran next to each other.

325
00:17:52,970 --> 00:17:56,804
以色列和约旦也坐同一排
Plus Israel and Jordan all sitting in the same pew.

326
00:17:56,970 --> 00:18:00,167
我们会引发第三次世界大战的
We'd be in danger of starting World War III.

327
00:18:00,330 --> 00:18:04,528
我知道爱尔兰也是I开头 可爱尔兰没用
I know Ireland begins with an I, but it doesn't make it any better.

328
00:18:04,690 --> 00:18:07,682
爱尔兰在任何事上都不起作用
Ireland doesn't make anything any better.

329
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:09,330
对了 传达所有人
If the papal envoy says,

330
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:11,036
要是教皇特使说"本座要净手"
"We desire to wash our hands",

331
00:18:11,036 --> 00:18:12,682
就是说他要上厕所
it means he wants a pee.

332
00:18:13,810 --> 00:18:17,644
对 "本座"是尊称 坐的是皇家宝厕(同花顺)
Yes, a royal "we", followed by a royal flush.

333
00:18:18,610 --> 00:18:20,805
小心提防南非人
Watch out for the South Africans.

334
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:25,282
人权问题?      不 他们想倾销柚子
human rights? No, they're trying to unload grapefruit.

335
00:18:25,450 --> 00:18:29,238
伯纳 皇宫问红毡铺地会不会有问题
The palace wants to know about the red carpets.

336
00:18:29,410 --> 00:18:32,217
女王担心象牙海岸(非洲)总统
The Ivory Coast wishes to award Her Majesty

337
00:18:32,217 --> 00:18:34,686
想向女王赠送大象勋章
with the Order of the Elephant.

338
00:18:34,686 --> 00:18:36,844
别挂 格拉汉 不能再扯进什么动物了
Hang on. We can't have another animal,

339
00:18:36,844 --> 00:18:38,205
尤其是大象
especially an elephant.

340
00:18:38,410 --> 00:18:41,880
白厅 内政部 外交部和卫生部
Whitehall, the Home Office, Foreign Office, the DHSS,

341
00:18:42,050 --> 00:18:44,697
都为一条小狗头疼一周了
have been tied up with one puppy for nearly a week!

342
00:18:44,697 --> 00:18:47,057
政府都瘫痪了 不许要大象
No elephants!

343
00:18:47,057 --> 00:18:50,401
不 塞浦路斯大主教不叫至圣宗座
The mode of address to a Cypriot archbishop is not Your Ecstasy,

344
00:18:50,401 --> 00:18:52,031
叫至福圣座
it's Your Beatitude.

345
00:18:52,031 --> 00:18:55,120
老天爷 又搞什么...
For God's sake, what is it...

346
00:18:55,290 --> 00:18:58,441
哦 抱歉 首相 我马上来
Oh, sorry, Prime Minister. I'll come in straight away.

347
00:19:05,370 --> 00:19:08,919
这是什么 伯纳?      海峡隧道的档案 首相
What on earth is that? The Channel Tunnel file.

348
00:19:09,090 --> 00:19:12,287
不 那一本呢?      小狗的档案
No, no, the other one. That's the puppy file.

349
00:19:14,650 --> 00:19:19,041
大致怎么说?      重量是3.5磅
Where have we got to? It weighed in at three and a half pounds.

350
00:19:19,210 --> 00:19:21,565
小狗?      不 档案
The puppy? No, the file.

351
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:24,449
怎么回事?      眼下我们已照会法国
What's happening? We've told the French

352
00:19:24,610 --> 00:19:26,896
说机场保安不得不
that airport security will have to

353
00:19:26,896 --> 00:19:28,973
把狗留在机场检疫
keep the puppy in quarantine.

354
00:19:28,973 --> 00:19:30,881
他们怎么说?      还没回复
What do they say? No reply yet.

355
00:19:31,050 --> 00:19:31,752
我们还指出
It is on the route

356
00:19:31,752 --> 00:19:33,563
机场在皇宫去温莎城堡途中
from the palace to Windsor,

357
00:19:33,563 --> 00:19:35,863
女王可以顺便去看看它
so the Queen could visit it.

358
00:19:35,863 --> 00:19:38,295
隔离中的狗能看吗?      如果不行
Can you visit quarantined dogs? Well, if she can't,

359
00:19:38,295 --> 00:19:41,231
她可以从车上朝它挥挥手吧
she can sort of wave to it.

360
00:19:43,010 --> 00:19:44,785
你说他们会作何反应?
What do you think they'll do?

361
00:19:44,785 --> 00:19:47,004
我想他们会威胁爆给媒体
Threaten to publish the story

362
00:19:47,004 --> 00:19:48,806
除非我们在海峡隧道上让步
if we don't give in on the tunnel.

363
00:19:48,970 --> 00:19:52,565
首相 我有紧急消息      希望是好消息
I have urgent news. I hope it's good news.

364
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:56,325
是也不是 警方在法国使馆区发现了炸弹
Yes and no. The police found a bomb in the French embassy grounds.

365
00:19:56,970 --> 00:20:01,168
什么? 谁放的?      还不知道
What?! Who put it there? We don't know yet.

366
00:20:01,330 --> 00:20:05,039
很多人都有动机      我就算一个
Lots of people could have a motive. Me, for a start.

367
00:20:06,290 --> 00:20:09,088
幸好被我们找到了...是好事吧
It's a good thing we found it... I suppose.

368
00:20:09,250 --> 00:20:13,562
另一条消息更糟 法国总统不飞过来了
The President is not flying in for the funeral.

369
00:20:13,730 --> 00:20:17,928
太好了      他不坐飞机 改坐车了 秘密入境
That's marvellous! He's not flying, he's driving! Secretly!

370
00:20:18,090 --> 00:20:21,799
拿专机作安全掩护      好主意
The plane is just going to be a decoy. Good idea.

371
00:20:21,970 --> 00:20:25,360
绝妙的主意 他可以带狗进来了      不行
A brilliant idea! He can bring the puppy! No!

372
00:20:25,530 --> 00:20:30,126
首相 您要授权把总统专车拦下搜查吗?
give permission for his car to be stopped and searched?

373
00:20:30,290 --> 00:20:33,241
您难道要侵犯他们的外交豁免权
Will you violate their diplomatic immunity and

374
00:20:33,241 --> 00:20:35,151
搜查外交邮袋?
search the diplomatic bag?

375
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:37,297
他们总不能把狗藏袋子里吧
Even they wouldn't put a puppy in a bag.

376
00:20:37,297 --> 00:20:39,052
会变成狗食袋(餐馆打包袋)
It'd be a doggy bag.

377
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:45,202
要是真搜出来 那可捅马蜂窝了
If we found it, that'd put the cat among the pigeons.

378
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:48,089
纵狗出袋了
Let the dog out of the bag.

379
00:20:48,250 --> 00:20:50,963
对 可是首相 万一车里没有狗呢?
But just suppose it wasn't there?

380
00:20:50,963 --> 00:20:53,022
对 我不能冒这个险
Yeah. I can't take the risk.

381
00:20:53,022 --> 00:20:54,551
可如果狗在里面
If it was there,

382
00:20:54,551 --> 00:20:56,886
他们就可以开进法国大使馆
they'll drive into the French embassy

383
00:20:56,886 --> 00:21:01,640
狗就进入了法国领土 在伦敦正中央
and that puppy will be on French territory here

384
00:21:01,810 --> 00:21:05,803
悬在我们头顶上      希望它懂规矩吧
Hanging over our heads. Better pray it's house-trained.

385
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:20,198
首相 真抱歉 能失陪一下吗?
I'm so sorry, would you excuse the Prime Minister?

386
00:21:21,330 --> 00:21:23,443
首相 我们有麻烦了
We have a problem.

387
00:21:23,443 --> 00:21:26,049
您跟法国总统说上话了吗?
Have you spoken to the French President yet?

388
00:21:26,049 --> 00:21:28,762
就说了几句套话      具体是什么?
A couple of well-chosen words. What, precisely?

389
00:21:28,930 --> 00:21:30,921
就是"您好"(法语)
Bonsoir, actually.

390
00:21:31,850 --> 00:21:33,804
首相 您不能不理他
You can't put it off.

391
00:21:33,804 --> 00:21:36,636
不然他又多一个被冒犯的借口了
It'll be one more thing for him to take offence at.

392
00:21:36,636 --> 00:21:38,201
他没这么容易被冒犯吧?
He can't be that easily offended, can he?

393
00:21:38,370 --> 00:21:40,524
当然没有 不过据我们所知
No, but in exchange

394
00:21:40,524 --> 00:21:42,570
要想让他们放弃狗的事
for dropping this dog nonsense,

395
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:45,879
他们想要全部隧道主权 从3海里领海算起
they want sovereignty over the tunnel from the three-mile limit.

396
00:21:46,050 --> 00:21:48,280
岂有此理      这是谈判开价
Absurd. That's the negotiating position.

397
00:21:48,450 --> 00:21:52,443
实际上他们同意五五开 从中间算
They'll concede to a 50-50 split midway across the Channel

398
00:21:52,610 --> 00:21:55,397
只要我们同意用法语作第一语言
if we agree to French as the first language on all

399
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:58,680
路标 告示 菜单 所有东西
signs, information, menus, everything.

400
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:01,562
都先法后英      我非得让步吗?
French comes before English. Must I concede?

401
00:22:01,730 --> 00:22:05,928
如果您想要奠基礼的话      好吧 他在哪?
If you want your foundation-stone ceremony. All right. Where is he?

402
00:22:06,090 --> 00:22:07,733
哈克夫人 您见过联合国
Mrs Hacker, have you met

403
00:22:07,733 --> 00:22:10,031
教科文组织的贝林杰先生了吗?
Monsieur Berenger from UNESCO?

404
00:22:10,450 --> 00:22:12,750
幸会       夫人 葬礼太棒了
Such a good funeral.

405
00:22:12,750 --> 00:22:14,109
比安德罗波夫(苏共书记)的强多了
Much better than Andropov's.

406
00:22:14,109 --> 00:22:17,320
他们太郁闷了      您喜欢就好
That was gloomy. So glad you're enjoying it.

407
00:22:17,490 --> 00:22:21,483
首相 有空吗?      这位是美国副总统
Prime Minister, got a minute? The American Vice President.

408
00:22:21,650 --> 00:22:23,435
哦 副总统先生      我刚跟苏联人聊完
I was talking to the Soviets.

409
00:22:23,435 --> 00:22:26,009
葛罗米柯的波兰笑话太好笑了
Gromyko's got a great Polish joke.

410
00:22:26,009 --> 00:22:29,241
什么这么好笑?      雅鲁泽尔斯基(波兰总统)
What is it? Jaruzelski!

411
00:22:32,530 --> 00:22:37,320
警察厅长 这位是联合国教科文的贝林杰先生
can I introduce you to Monsieur Berenger from UNESCO?

412
00:22:37,490 --> 00:22:41,085
教科文? 对对 不错的小国家
UNESCO? Ah, yes. Gallant little country.

413
00:22:43,090 --> 00:22:47,163
汉弗莱爵士      您记得苏联大使吧
Ah, Sir Humphrey! You remember the Soviet ambassador.

414
00:22:47,330 --> 00:22:52,484
我说 前首相的去世真让人痛心
the death of the past PM is a very sad occasion.

415
00:22:52,650 --> 00:22:57,246
对对 真痛心      可也不算英国的损失
Oh, yes, yes, very sad... But it is no loss for Britain.

416
00:22:58,690 --> 00:23:02,000
你知道他的问题在哪吗?
You know what his trouble was?

417
00:23:02,170 --> 00:23:05,640
他这里很厉害 这里很厉害...
He had plenty here, plenty here...

418
00:23:05,810 --> 00:23:07,846
可是这里不行
...but nothing here!

419
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:11,523
什么 伯纳?
Yes, Bernard?

420
00:23:11,690 --> 00:23:13,466
失陪了 副总统先生
Forgive me,

421
00:23:13,466 --> 00:23:15,403
我要去找法国朋友聊聊了
I must talk to our French friends.

422
00:23:15,403 --> 00:23:16,756
好 可我得跟您谈谈
I did want to talk to you about the

423
00:23:16,756 --> 00:23:18,600
北约的德国基地的事
NATO bases in Germany.

424
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:22,045
明天修道院里谈      一言为定
Tomorrow, Westminster Abbey. You got a deal.

425
00:23:22,210 --> 00:23:24,661
首相 您得看看这份安全档案
You need to see this security file.

426
00:23:24,661 --> 00:23:26,954
回头再说 伯纳 我要跟法国总统谈话了
I'm about to talk to the President.

427
00:23:26,954 --> 00:23:28,481
对 可您应该先看这份档案
You should see this file first.

428
00:23:28,650 --> 00:23:31,218
首相 法国大使馆的炸弹
That bomb in the French embassy

429
00:23:31,218 --> 00:23:32,908
是法国警方安放的
was planted by the French police.

430
00:23:32,908 --> 00:23:35,288
开玩笑吧? 为什么?
You're not serious? Why?

431
00:23:35,450 --> 00:23:38,764
为了试我们 证明我们保安不力
To catch us out, prove our security inefficient.

432
00:23:38,764 --> 00:23:41,809
非法偷运炸弹进入英国?
Smuggling explosives into the UK?

433
00:23:41,809 --> 00:23:43,201
正是      有证据吗?
Correct. Got proof?

434
00:23:43,370 --> 00:23:46,672
在他们旅馆找到了配套的雷管 他们招了
We found a detonator in their hotel.

435
00:23:46,672 --> 00:23:48,227
太好了
This is wonderful!

436
00:23:48,227 --> 00:23:50,334
汉弗莱 我先跟总统谈两分钟
Give me two minutes alone with the President.

437
00:23:50,334 --> 00:23:53,331
看我打手势 就送档案进来
When I give you a signal, bring that file in.

438
00:23:53,730 --> 00:23:55,880
首相 用什么手势?
What will the signal be?

439
00:24:02,130 --> 00:24:05,725
万分抱歉 总统先生 我保证他马上就到
I'm so sorry, Monsieur le President. I'm sure he's just coming.

440
00:24:05,890 --> 00:24:09,200
总统先生...海峡隧道的事
Monsieur le President... the tunnel.

441
00:24:09,370 --> 00:24:15,081
隧道 没错 但首先 能不能先澄清个小误会
can we clear up this misunderstanding about the puppy

442
00:24:15,250 --> 00:24:18,003
关于我明天向女王赠狗的事?
which I am presenting to Her Majesty tomorrow?

443
00:24:18,170 --> 00:24:20,206
据我所知 真对不起
I'm very sorry,

444
00:24:20,206 --> 00:24:22,394
我不能要求女王打破法律
but I can't ask her to break the law.

445
00:24:22,394 --> 00:24:24,517
我没要女王打破法律
I do not want the Queen to break the law

446
00:24:24,517 --> 00:24:27,781
我只要首相给打个折就行
I merely want the PM to bend it.

447
00:24:27,781 --> 00:24:30,965
实在很对不起 我向您郑重道歉
I'm deeply sorry. If I possibly could.

448
00:24:31,130 --> 00:24:33,836
要是法国人民听说了
If the French people learn of this rejection,

449
00:24:33,836 --> 00:24:36,015
这可是照国家脸上打了一耳光...
a national slap in the face...

450
00:24:37,130 --> 00:24:40,964
隧道      隧道? 你给我出难题了
The tunnel. The tunnel? You make it difficult for me.

451
00:24:41,130 --> 00:24:44,600
法国人可不能再挨第二耳光了
The French will not accept a second slap in the face

452
00:24:44,770 --> 00:24:47,653
您还拒绝了我们合情合理的
and you are rejecting our very reasonable proposal

453
00:24:47,653 --> 00:24:50,216
多佛港以外全归法国的建议
for French sovereignty as far as Dover.

454
00:24:50,930 --> 00:24:53,490
不过 这个先不谈
However, setting that to one side,

455
00:24:53,650 --> 00:24:58,678
还有个问题 哪种语言做第一语言?
there is the question of which shall be la langue de preference

456
00:24:58,850 --> 00:25:03,446
汉弗莱爵士 我刚看到明天的典礼安排
Sir Humphrey, I have just seen this order of service for tomorrow.

457
00:25:03,610 --> 00:25:06,363
太让人尴尬了 看这圣歌
It is deeply embarrassing. This hymn.

458
00:25:07,370 --> 00:25:11,921
"施洗者泪洒约旦河岸"(1736)? 怎么啦?
"On Jordan's Bank, The Baptist's Cry"? Why?

459
00:25:12,090 --> 00:25:16,288
您不知道约旦河岸昨天被炸了吗?
Don't you know the Jordan Bank went bust yesterday?

460
00:25:17,490 --> 00:25:21,280
当然 我们可以一半用法语在前
Surely, if we have half the signs in French first

461
00:25:21,280 --> 00:25:23,007
一半用英语...
and half the signs in English...

462
00:25:23,650 --> 00:25:26,642
公平吧?      这不合逻辑
...that's fair? It's not logical.

463
00:25:27,650 --> 00:25:31,928
逻辑重要吗?      法律重要吗?
Does logic matter? Does law matter?

464
00:25:32,090 --> 00:25:36,686
当然 全欧洲就剩英国还...没有狂犬病
Yes. Britain is the only country in Europe still... free of rabies.

465
00:25:38,290 --> 00:25:41,168
真抱歉 伯纳会跟你商量的 伯纳
Bernard will handle this for you. Bernard...

466
00:25:42,970 --> 00:25:44,925
总统先生 打扰一下好吗?
Monsieur le President, will you forgive me?

467
00:25:44,925 --> 00:25:48,069
首相 请您赶紧看看这个
Prime Minister, I think you ought to see this.

468
00:25:50,130 --> 00:25:52,724
不会吧 我不信
No, I don't believe it!

469
00:25:53,970 --> 00:25:57,679
总统先生 我必须请您解释一下
Mr President, I shall have to ask you to explain this.

470
00:26:00,090 --> 00:26:04,561
这件事有多严重 不用我说了吧
I need hardly say how grave this matter is.

471
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:08,769
首相 请您相信我对此一无所知
Prime Minister, I ask you to believe I had no knowledge of this.

472
00:26:08,930 --> 00:26:12,366
国宾代表团企图陷害我国政府?
An attempt by a guest to deceive our government?

473
00:26:12,530 --> 00:26:14,885
偷运爆炸物进入英国?
Smuggling explosives into the UK?

474
00:26:15,050 --> 00:26:18,290
可您得知道 法国政府从来不知道
You must know that the French government never knows

475
00:26:18,290 --> 00:26:20,511
法国警方在干什么啊
what French security are doing.

476
00:26:22,330 --> 00:26:26,482
您不能为他们负责?      不 我不是这个意思
You can't take responsibility for them? That's not what I mean.

477
00:26:26,650 --> 00:26:29,847
可如果报告属实 请接受我衷心的道歉
If this report is true, accept my profound regrets.

478
00:26:30,010 --> 00:26:34,208
恐怕确实属实      谢谢 首相
It's true enough, I'm afraid. Thank you, Prime Minister.

479
00:26:34,370 --> 00:26:37,900
您看 这下首相就很难处理...
It makes it so difficult for the Prime Minister...

480
00:26:37,900 --> 00:26:39,289
海峡隧道的事了
over the Channel Tunnel.

481
00:26:39,289 --> 00:26:43,003
炸弹的事捅出去 英国人民就不肯让步了
the British will want to make few concessions.

482
00:26:43,170 --> 00:26:46,367
他们不知道能不能安全...通过
They won't know whether it's safe to... go through.

483
00:26:46,530 --> 00:26:49,966
没准里面全是法国官方炸弹      可不是
It could be full of official French bombs. Absolument.

484
00:26:51,010 --> 00:26:54,400
当然 为维护英法两国友谊
Of course, in the interests of Anglo-French friendship,

485
00:26:54,570 --> 00:26:57,960
我们可以忽略你们保安人员的罪行
we could overlook the crimes of your security men.

486
00:26:58,130 --> 00:27:02,521
我说...主权对半分吧?
I suppose... sovereignty halfway across?

487
00:27:02,690 --> 00:27:05,488
我得把这写下来 可以吗
I'll just write that down, if I may.

488
00:27:06,330 --> 00:27:09,931
一半标志先英后法 奠基礼定在两个月后
Half the signs in English first and the ceremony in two months...

489
00:27:09,931 --> 00:27:11,679
在多佛举行
in Dover.

490
00:27:11,770 --> 00:27:17,561
以表达两国间永恒的亲密和信任
As an expression of the trust between our two countries.

491
00:27:18,370 --> 00:27:21,168
我们明天就草拟公报吧 好吗 汉弗莱?
Let us have a draft communiqu?tomorrow.

492
00:27:21,330 --> 00:27:23,480
(法语)是 首相
Mais oui, Prime Minister.

493
00:27:25,253 --> 00:27:30,570
